  "strategy": "1. Approach and rationale\nThe current method relies on gradient descent with projection, which might struggle due to non-convexity. Instead, we'll adopt a mixed-integer approach using binary variables to model h as a piecewise constant function. This allows exact constraint handling and discrete optimization of interval values.\n\n2. Mathematical specification\n- Decision variables: h_i \u2208 {0, 1} for interval i (binary)\n- Objective: Minimize max_k Overlap(k; h)\n- Overlap(k) = sum_{i} h_i * (1 - h_{i+k}) * w_i, where w_i is interval width\n- Constraints: sum(h_i * w_i) = 1, h_i \u2208 {0,1}\n\n3. Implementation procedure\na. Split [0,2] into intervals of width dx\nb. For each k, compute Overlap(k)\nc. Find binary h minimizing max Overlap(k)\nd. Solve via mixed-integer programming\n\n4. Search choices\n- Initialize with parent h\n- Use GLPK solver for integer LP\n- Discretize shifts to fixed grid\n\n5. Compute budget\nDomestic costs: Integer programming with n_points=45, 45 variables, 45 shifts. Solve via GLPK's optimization.\n\n6. Validation\nVerify sum(h)*dx=1, h \u2208 {0,1}, evaluate overlap",
